 "summary": "A family of glass-passivated silicon transient voltage suppressors in the axial-lead 1.5KE case, rated to absorb a 1500 W peak pulse of 10/1000 µs shape. Breakdown voltages run from 6.8 V to 540 V in the unidirectional A types and from 6.8 V to 220 V in the bidirectional CA types; types 6.8 V to 200 V also carry JEDEC numbers 1N6267A to 1N6303A. 1.5KE20CA-E3/54 is the bidirectional 20 V type: 17.1 V stand-off, 19.0 V to 21.0 V breakdown at 1 mA, and 27.7 V maximum clamping at 54.2 A, commercial grade on 13-inch tape and reel.",
