 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Ratings and pulse shape",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 1500 W rating is for a 10/1000 µs pulse repeated at no more than 0.01 % duty cycle; the PPPM and IPPM limits in the tables are for a single pulse starting at 25 °C. Fig. 1 trades peak power against pulse width: about 1.5 kW at 1 ms, rising for shorter pulses. Fig. 2 takes peak power and current linearly from 100 % at 25 °C to zero at 175 °C initial junction temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Bidirectional types",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A CA suffix in place of A gives the bidirectional version, made from 6.8 V to 220 V (for example 1.5KE220CA). Its electrical limits are the A type's, applied in both polarities. Forward surge current and forward voltage ratings belong to unidirectional types only."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Steady dissipation",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "With 9.5 mm (0.375 in) leads the part dissipates 6.5 W up to a lead temperature of 75 °C, falling linearly to zero at 175 °C (Fig. 5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Response and use",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Clamping begins within about 1 ns on bidirectional parts. The parts suit protection of ICs, MOSFETs, hybrids and sensor signal lines against transients from inductive load switching and lightning, including lightning induced on rural or remote lines (R.E.A. P.E. 60). Several may be wired in series or in parallel to raise the peak power handled."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The -E3 suffix is the RoHS commercial grade; HE3 is RoHS and AEC-Q101 qualified, available from 6.8 V to 220 V in A and CA types. UL 497B recognition (file E136766) covers 1.5KE6.8A to 1.5KE220A and the matching CA types."
  }
 ],
